Subject: [PATCH] Add Topic to Video engine to the Video Studio
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A fourth Video Studio engine: give a topic and get a finished narrated
short — AI script (tenant's text model via the textGen routing layer),
stock footage from Pexels/Pixabay (admin-keyed, encrypted at rest, env
fallback), sentence-timed TTS narration (OpenAI audio integration),
burned subtitles, optional background music, all composed with the same
system ffmpeg the slideshow engine uses.

Pipeline design ported from MoneyPrinterTurbo (MIT) and reimplemented
natively: one LLM call returns script + ordered search terms;
per-sentence TTS gives exact subtitle cues from WAV headers with no
transcription step; scenes cycle downloaded clips, cover-cropped to the
target aspect.

Wired end-to-end through the existing patterns: engine enum in the
OpenAPI spec (+ regenerated clients), video quota/credit funding
untouched, jobRunner branch, /admin/stock-sources/{id}/key endpoints,
videoGen kill switch inherited, tenant-scoped music input, and a new
Topic to Video tab in the studio with voice/length/subtitles controls.

Verified: full typecheck clean; api-server 1046/1046 (22 new, incl.
real-ffmpeg composition encodes), web 304/304 (2 new), mobile 149/149;
spec lint + codegen drift clean; db push clean against Postgres 16.

